      "explanation": "A base-ten logarithm asks which power of \\(10\\) equals its argument. Since \\(10^2=100\\), we have \\(\\log_{10}100=2\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\left[\\log_{10}\\left(5\\log_{10}100\\right)\\right]^2\n=\\left[\\log_{10}(10)\\right]^2\n=1^2=1.\n\\]\nBoth logarithm arguments are positive, so the expression is defined. The value is \\(\\boxed{1}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
